<h2>Launch, Funding &amp; Team Plan (added 2026-09-25)</h2>
<p class="updated">Strategy: publish RESULTS now, keep the RECIPE (training code, data mix, hyperparameters, failed-experiment log) private until v4 (1B); then open the architecture code + small weights. Glenn = founder/President/Chief Scientist; son (ML/AI expert) = CEO &amp; public face once the plan + early traction exist. Status: TO-DO unless marked.</p>
<p><b>Phase 0 &mdash; credibility (weeks 0&ndash;3)</b></p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Fixed matched-transformer baseline</b> at 363M (same data/tokens, <code>attn_single_residual: true</code>) &mdash; the old &ldquo;spiking beats transformer 34%&rdquo; claim is INVALID (double-residual bug). #1 experiment for the story. <b>Also retract the 34% / energy numbers in <code>marketing_blurbs.html</code> until re-measured.</b></li>
  <li><b>One crisp, measured win</b>, rigorously: persistent memory across turns/sessions, recall per parameter under split-replay, or spike sparsity/ops-per-token (energy <i>potential</i>, not GPU energy).</li>
  <li><b>Honest comparison vs public small models</b> (SmolLM2-360M, Qwen2.5-0.5B), stated per training token (they saw ~400&times; more).</li>
  <li><b>Licence check</b> before publishing: Llama-3 tokenizer + Llama-3.2-3B teacher (KD/OPD) &rarr; Llama licence naming/attribution rules. Lawyer to confirm.</li>
</ul>
<ul>
  <li><b>Update marketing blurbs</b> (<code>H:\Projects\PsycorAI - Backup\blogs\marketing_blurbs.html</code>) ONLY after the fixed transformer comparison + Phase 0 tests are complete and solid &mdash; replace the invalid 34%/energy claims with the re-measured numbers.</li>
  <li><b>Brains as a unique selling point</b> (Glenn 2026-09-25): test brains rigorously after post-training (bake on the final checkpoint; domain-specificity matrix vs no-brain; exposure-length sweep 1k/10k/100k tokens; task test e.g. tools brain on <code>tool_eval</code>; save/load across sessions). If effective, useful and compelling &rarr; make them the lead of the demo, tech report and launch (&ldquo;load a brain&rdquo; in the HF Space, &ldquo;build a brain&rdquo; tutorials). If not &rarr; don't claim them.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Phase 1 &mdash; company + soft launch (weeks 2&ndash;6)</b></p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Incorporate</b> (US, Delaware C-corp is the investor default); assign existing code/IP to the company; founder vesting. Son: check his employer's IP/moonlighting agreement before he contributes.</li>
  <li><b>Provisional patent decision</b> (see 2026-09-25 chat): only if we have a measured, specific method worth claiming (e.g. baking/loading portable brains); must be filed BEFORE any public disclosure; micro-entity USPTO fee $65, attorney-drafted ~$3&ndash;6k.</li>
  <li><b>Tech report</b> (architecture at a high level + results + honest limits) &rarr; arXiv (needs an endorser with cs.LG papers: son if he has them, or a collaborator) + Psycor blog.</li>
  <li><b>Live demo</b>: Hugging Face Space with v3-chat (weights private), showcasing the brain feature. Short demo video. Posts: X, Hacker News, r/LocalLLaMA &mdash; led by the son.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Phase 2 &mdash; compute without dilution (parallel)</b></p>
<ul>
  <li>Apply: NVIDIA Inception, Microsoft for Startups (Azure credits $1k self-serve &rarr; $150k with VC/accelerator), Google Cloud for Startups (up to $350k, VC-backed tier), small grants (CloudRift $100&ndash;1k). NAIRR only via a US university/nonprofit partner.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Phase 3 &mdash; v4 (1B) + open the architecture (months 2&ndash;4)</b></p>
<ul>
  <li>Train v4 (cloud or 5090); release inference code + small open weights under a clear licence (e.g. Liquid-style: free under a revenue threshold); Discord; &ldquo;build a brain&rdquo; tutorials.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Phase 4 &mdash; team &amp; money (from month 2)</b></p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Team</b>: son joins as CEO; recruit 1&ndash;2 experts by collaborating first (co-author the eval paper with authors of the work we build on). YC co-founder matching as a backup.</li>
  <li><b>Money</b>: pre-seed from technical angels + AI accelerators once demo + report + one credible expert exist.</li>
</ul>

<h2>v4 &mdash; current work (results, fix list, demo, MoB)</h2>
<ol>
  <li><b>10-22 (Neuro 73, Glenn OK) 5080 BRAIN TRAINING SPEED &mdash; status: built + tested 10-22, used from brain_fdc_C on</b>: the LoRA trainer is CPU-bound (one thread at 100%, 5080 ~10-20% busy; more cores cannot help a single process). src/train_sft.py: (1) no GPU sync per micro-step (spike rate kept on the GPU), pinned non_blocking batch copies; (2) flag <code>lora_base_bf16</code> (default off): frozen base linears stored in bf16 (autocast casts them anyway) = ~2.2 GB less at 1B -&gt; B8 x GA4 on the 5080. 13L 20-step test (temp/n73_bf16_test.sh): loss + spike identical at every step, 342 -&gt; 407 tok/s on a shared GPU. Chain temp/n73_chain.sh (health B8, fallback B4, then merge tries; pause with <code>touch logs/n73.hold</code>). Ideas to-test: torch.compile / CUDA graphs for train_sft (launch-bound); batched quiz decoding.</li>
  <li><b>10-22 (Neuro 73, Glenn) MULTI-BRAIN: 2+ brains at once &mdash; status: (1) router BUILT 10-22 (CPU-tested temp/n73_test_router.py; live after Glenn's next server restart: brain menu &rarr; &ldquo;auto&rdquo;); (2) merge tries QUEUED behind the brain reruns (temp/n73_merge_tries.sh &rarr; logs/n73_merge_tries.log: sum 1/1, 0.5/0.5, 0.7/0.7, TIES k0.2, DARE-TIES d0.3; tool temp/n73_merge_brains.py); (3) STACKED + (4) JOINT queued 10-22 (Glenn OK) after the merge tries: temp/n73_after.sh &rarr; temp/n73_mb34.sh &rarr; logs/n73_mb34.log; (5) to-decide</b>: BDH paper 2509.26507 &sect;7.1 + App. B.4: one En-Es base (n 24,576, 19M) cloned, tuned on En-Fr and En-Pt (1.2B tok each), merged by CONCATENATING every neuron-dimension tensor (n -&gt; 49,152, 38M) and averaging embeddings / output head; no training after. Into-English held (loss 0.43 / 0.40 / 0.39), from-English degraded (1.45 / 0.77 / 0.86 vs ~0.33 for the specialists) and MIXES the three languages; "a small amount of training on all language pairs" fixes it (no numbers). Works because BDH neurons are positive, sparse (~5%) and fairly monosemantic, so concatenated neurons add little cross-talk. Ours so far: sum of two LoRA brains on the SAME base (n61d C2, 180k) = Python 0%, health 19.3%, ppl 289 (single brains 100% / 100%, ppl 36 / 70): plain merging fails because each brain is a large dense delta. Options, in order: (1) ROUTER = all brains loaded, auto-pick per turn from the existing guards (needs_python / needs_health), no merge, zero interference; (2) quick no-training merge tries on the new brains: scaled sum, TIES / DARE on the LoRA deltas (scripts/merge_ties_dare.py adapted); expected weak; (3) STACKED brains: train brain 2 on base + brain 1 merged, with brain-1 quiz rehearsal in its replay (the chat-brain path); (4) JOINT brain: one LoRA on Python + health data together (the honest &ldquo;merged&rdquo; upper bound); (5) BDH-STYLE NEURON BRAINS (research): a brain = extra relu2 FFN units (base frozen, new units silenced on replay text by an activation penalty), merge = concatenate units (exact, like BDH), then a short mixed tune; also smaller brains to cut the ppl cost.</li>
  <li><b>10-21 (Neuro 71, Glenn) ONLINE DEMO: answers for the REMOTE user's location &mdash; status: parked (for when the model goes online)</b>: time, weather and units must follow the visitor, not the server. Plan: the page sends the browser's time zone (<code>Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone</code>) and locale with every request; the city for "what's the weather?" from the browser's location permission (<code>navigator.geolocation</code>, the visitor says yes or no) or a server-side IP lookup (privacy notice needed); country -&gt; units (US / Liberia / Myanmar imperial, else metric); the location becomes per request (today one home location for the whole server). Builds on the local version below.</li>
  <li><b>10-21 (Neuro 71, Glenn) demo: local time / weather / units from this computer's location &mdash; status: built 10-21 (CPU-tested, <code>temp/n71_test_local.py</code>; live after a server restart; city to be set in <code>scripts/demo/home.json</code>, empty = Los Angeles from the time zone)</b>: <code>tools_exec.HOME</code>, <code>guards.local_time / local_weather</code> (whole-message patterns), route + ground, page chip "here: …". time zone from the system (America/Los_Angeles), country from <code>/usr/share/zoneinfo/zone.tab</code> (US), home city from a setting; "what time is it?" / "what's the weather?" with no place -&gt; local; weather unit default by country (F + mph in the US, else C + km/h) unless the question names one; boiling / melting points list the home unit first.</li>
  <li><b>10-21 (Neuro 71) demo code review &mdash; status: fixed 10-21 except (5) = knob <code>DEMO_BUCKET</code> (default 512 unchanged) -&gt; to-test: time 256 vs 512 on a free GPU, then pick the default; (9) left as is</b>: (1) Replay after the Memory test replays the turn BEFORE it (memtest does not set <code>ENG.last</code>); (2) every fixed reply is labelled "small talk"; (3) the offline switch does not cover <code>get_time</code> (a city not in the table goes to the online geocoder); (4) weather unit default differs (route F, tool C); (5) speed: every decode step runs a 512-token CUDA graph, the answer pass is ~100-250 tokens -&gt; a 256 bucket may be ~1.5-2x faster there (measure when a GPU is free); (6) page: <code>rgba()</code> reads the CSS colour per cell -&gt; draw 10.6 -&gt; 5.1 ms with a cached colour (measured, 86 columns); (7) <code>available_timezones()</code> 27 ms per call, up to 4 per time question; (8) raw mode: past 2,048 tokens the oldest text (incl. pasted word pairs) drops out silently; (9) <code>chunk_stream.py</code> unused by the v2 engine (kept).</li>
  <li><b>10-21 (Neuro 71, Glenn) demo HONESTY guards &mdash; status: built (CPU-checked; live after Glenn's next server restart)</b>: <code>guards.gibberish</code> -&gt; "I don't understand." (mostly non-English words; 0 / 6,000 tools + 1 / 6,000 coldstart prompts flagged, <code>temp/n71_gibberish_fp.py</code>); <code>guards.python_untaught</code> (function name not in <code>scripts/demo/python_functions.json</code>, Python brain on) and the health reply -&gt; "That is not part of my training set."; <code>guards.off_topic</code> (search article that does not mention the asked name, e.g. "Zorbania") and failed search / define / weather -&gt; "I didn't find that information." (24 live searches: 3 / 3 made-up names caught, 0 / 21 real false alarms, <code>temp/n71_search_probe.sh</code>); <code>_place</code> no longer runs into the next sentence ("Sydney. What's"). Tests <code>temp/n71_test_honesty.py</code>, <code>temp/n71_prompt_check.py</code>. Prompt list <code>docs/demo_prompts_2026_10_21.md</code>.</li>
  <li><b>10-21 (Neuro 71) demo search: wrong article for some names &mdash; status: to-fix</b>: "Treaty of Westphalia" -&gt; the region "Westphalia" (no date; the article is "Peace of Westphalia"); "Moonlight Sonata" -&gt; the 1937 film. The model then answers from an article without the fact. Idea: prefer a title holding all the query's capitalised words, then a non-film title.</li>
  <li><b>10-21 (Neuro 72) v4f THROUGHPUT LEVERS</b> &mdash; status: researched, to-build on Glenn's OK. Facts: 5090 kernel-busy 86.5% (40 s, <code>temp/n72_util.sh</code>) = ~13% idle; CPU i7-5820K + WSL = launch-bound parts; PCIe 3.0 x8; MFU ~47% of 209.5 TFLOPS. Math-preserving: (1) <b>GLENN OK 10-21 (if fair + ~1 day)</b>: build + test before phase B (~10-26), KD phase: Llama teacher on the 5080 one micro ahead (frees VRAM -> B4xGA4), est. 8.9k -> ~12k tok/s = ~1 day saved, 5080 busy ~3 days; [10-22 BUILT (default off): src/kd.py RemoteTeacher + config <code>kd_remote: &lt;socket&gt;</code> in train_gpu (one micro ahead, same windows in the same order) + server temp/kd_teacher_server.py on the 5080; wire test PASS (temp/n73_kd_proto_test.py); 150M local-vs-remote 30-step loss test queued (temp/n73_kd_test.sh, after the 5080 brain work). The KD phase starts with only GPU 0 visible, so the teacher is a separate process. DEPLOY before dense ends (~10-26 21:00): start the server on the 5080 + add kd_remote to configs/v4std_conv.yaml (keep B2xGA8: no VRAM risk; the teacher compute leaves the 5090)] (2) plain MQAR aux in 1-2 passes, not 16 splits, est. 3-6%; (3) NorMuon: compiled / foreach elementwise + addmm in Newton-Schulz, est. 2-4%; (4) pinned non-blocking batch copies (~6 host syncs / step), est. 0.5-2%; (5) cuDNN vs flash SDPA bench on sm_120, est. 0-3%; (6) Liger fused linear CE, est. 1-3%. Parked: Gram Newton-Schulz / symmetric GEMM (kernels for H100/B200, numerics), CUDA graphs (grad accumulation), FP8 / batch / NS-step changes (recipe), native Linux. Deploy = one ~30 min stop at a ckpt: profile + flags on, before/after tok/s.</li>
<li><b>10-21 (Neuro 70, Glenn) CHAT BRAIN = Option 1 &mdash; status: to-build NEXT SESSION</b>: multi-turn LoRA brain on <code>sft_v4_final_slim</code> (recipe <code>temp/n62_brain.sh</code>, 5080, ~3 h) from teacher-written (Llama-3.2-3B) multi-turn chats: follow-ups ("tell me another one", pronouns, "what did I say earlier") MIXED with tool calls (history broke tool use, n66: DEMO_HISTORY off) + replay; quiz = held-out follow-ups + tool score; demo: brain on + history on. Only when WSL RAM allows (not beside v4f + demo). First check: history on with the current model (joke example). <b>Plan 10-21 (Neuro 71, Glenn: go, 5080 free): status: to-build</b>: (1) prompt format: earlier turns in a <code>### Conversation:</code> block as <code>User: … / Assistant: &lt;final reply&gt;</code> (no ANSWER/TOOL words), current turn in the trained <code>### Instruction</code> format; tool-result pass gets the block too (engine <code>_assistant_prompt</code> + second pass, behind <code>DEMO_HISTORY</code>); (2) baseline = new format on <code>sft_v4_final_slim</code>, no training, same quiz; (3) data ~7k 2-4-turn chats: teacher follow-ups (another one, pronouns, recall of user facts, corrections) + TEMPLATED tool follow-ups with gold args from history ("what about Paris?", "convert that to miles") + topic switches + 1:1 single-turn replay (tools + self-knowledge); (4) train last turn only, target slid over turns (Mellum2), <code>n62_brain.sh</code> recipe with <code>sft_max_len</code> 256 -&gt; 512; (5) quiz 300 held-out chats: follow-up correctness, history-arg tool correctness, tools after topic switch; single-turn <code>tool_eval</code> within 2 pts. Limit: one brain at a time (chat brain excludes python / health). <b>10-21 Neuro 72: plan v2</b> <code>docs/chat_brain_plan_2026_10_21.md</code> &mdash; status: step 1 format built, baseline done (history 8/21, alone 5/21; topic switch keeps tools 5/5 = n66 bug fixed by the format; facts / another-one / pronouns 0 = need training); history-aware guards prototyped <code>temp/n72_proto/</code> (10/21); loader split-key bug; answer pass = last turn only; DEMO_BUCKET default 256 (-33% time); step 6 = merge + retrain python / health brains on the chat base. <b>10-21 16:50: steps 1-3 done</b> (shared formatter, split fix, history-aware guards + tests, data study 23k / answer 9.8k / quiz 302); <b>step 4 training</b> <code>temp/n72_chat_brain.sh</code> (B2xGA16: B4 = 5080 'device not ready'), quiz + tool_eval chained. <b>RESULT 10-21 23:35: brain_chat held-out quiz 90.1% (base 26.5%), hand 19/21 (11/21); tool_eval mode .980 tool .984 args .902 refuse .962 (base .975/.992/.902/.949) = PASS.</b> Demo: --brain chat=brain_chat (history turns on with it). <b>10-22 00:50 step 6a done:</b> merged base <code>sft_v4_chat</code> + backup <code>sft_v4_chat_backup</code> (identical); quiz on the merged base = 90.1% / hand 19/21 (same as brain on). 10-22 retrain python / health brains on sft_v4_chat: GLENN OK, both FAILED at start on the 5080 (py B4 OOM, fdc B8 device not ready) -> rerun smaller micro-batch (py B2xGA16, fdc B4xGA8; edit temp/n72_brains_chat.sh); demo with --run sft_v4_chat needs DEMO_HISTORY=1.</li>
  <li><b>10-21 (Neuro 70, Glenn) PLAIN-LANGUAGE MEMORY ACROSS CHUNKS = Option 2 &mdash; status: parked for v5</b>: SFT / training examples &gt;1,024 tokens whose answer is only in the earlier chunk (natural sentences, not token-range MQAR; today ~chance); needs longer sequences + new data; research-grade.</li>
  <li><b>10-20 15:50 (Neuro 70) demo search: misspelled names</b> &mdash; built: <code>guards.ground</code> replaces a search query that drops a capitalised name of the question with the question's topic (fuzzy, so "Einstein" for "Einstien" is kept); <code>tools_exec.search</code> matches a title the query nearly spells ("Treaty of Versaille") when none is named exactly. Tested 9 questions (<code>temp/n70_spell_probe.py</code>). Takes effect on Glenn's next demo-server restart. <b>built 10-20:</b> "capital of France" picked "Capital (French magazine)" -&gt; a one-word title now counts as named only when the query capitalises it, and the near-spelling match needs a multi-word title (now: List of capitals of France = Paris; "moon distance" = Lunar distance). 15 questions checked (<code>temp/n70_spell_probe.py</code>, <code>temp/n70_hits_probe2.py</code>). <b>built 10-20:</b> boiling / melting point + density added to the measured-fact path (tools_exec + guards.route); "what is the &lt;measure&gt; of Y" searches Y (was the film "Boiling Point" / article "Density"). Tungsten now gives 5,930 °C. <b>built 10-20:</b> measure not in the intro -&gt; Wikidata (boiling/melting point, density; preferred or single value, °C+°F / g/cm3; iron = 1,538 °C, the article text only gives pig iron) -&gt; whole article -&gt; else a failed result "the Wikipedia article X does not give the Y" (chocolate). "How old/tall/far is Y" also searches Y (Eiffel Tower found the film). 15 more questions checked (<code>temp/n70_hits_probe4.py</code>). <b>built 10-20:</b> market-prediction questions ("What will the stock market do next week?" -&gt; CAPE "expected to be higher") get a fixed backend reply in <code>guards._SOCIAL</code> (no prediction / no investment advice); 19 cases checked (<code>temp/n70_market_probe.py</code>). <b>built 10-20:</b> "Order a pizza" sent "I got the pizza" to "the team" -&gt; fixed backend reply for order/buy/book/reserve/pay/call/hire/rent requests; send_message is dropped unless the question asks for a message (message/text/tell/email/write/send/notify/let X know). 19 cases checked (<code>temp/n70_action_probe.py</code>). <b>built 10-20 (Glenn):</b> a request to write Python code with the Python brain off gets the fixed backend reply "I don't have the Python skill loaded. Turn on the Python brain and ask again." (<code>guards.needs_python</code> / <code>PY_OFF</code>, checked in <code>engine.assistant</code>); 15 cases checked (<code>temp/n70_py_probe.py</code>). <b>built 10-20 (Glenn):</b> health brain ON + an amount question (protein / calories / carbs) about a food it was not taught (beef -&gt; 3 g, 2 g, 4.2 g invented) or a cooked / dried one -&gt; fixed backend reply "That food isn't in my health brain..." (<code>guards.untaught_food</code>, list <code>scripts/demo/health_foods.json</code> = the 150 taught foods of health_sk_F, made by <code>temp/n70_mk_health_foods.py</code>; a new health brain needs a new list); 19 cases checked (<code>temp/n70_health_probe.py</code>). <b>built 10-20 (Glenn):</b> health brain off, "How much protein ... raw pumpkin" -&gt; Pumpkin intro had no figure, model said "100 grams of protein" -&gt; <code>tools_exec._nutrition</code>: protein / calories / carbs / fat amount questions search the food alone and read the whole article's nutrition line ("x% protein" = x g per 100 g; "100 g ... N kilocalories"), else a failed result "the Wikipedia article Beef does not give ..."; 10 cases + all earlier search tests pass (<code>temp/n70_nutr_probe.py</code>). Caveat: some articles give COOKED values (Lentil = boiled 9%); the quote keeps "Boiled". <b>built 10-20:</b> "time in California" -&gt; model called America/New_York and "California" was unknown, so ground() could not repair it -&gt; <code>tools_exec._TZ</code> + 50 US states (two-zone states = the zone most people live in) + ~40 countries; any other place via the Open-Meteo geocoder's timezone (result names the place found: "Narnia, Bangladesh"); "EST"/"PST" now map to the DST-aware city zones (was the fixed UTC-5 "EST"). 18 cases checked (<code>temp/n70_time_probe.py</code>). <b>built 10-20 (Glenn):</b> "What time does the NYSE open tomorrow?" -&gt; intro had no time, model said 11:00 AM -&gt; <code>tools_exec._answer_sentence</code>: for when / what time / what year / how many / how long questions whose intro has NO number of that kind, the best sentence (right kind of number + question words, non-title words x3) from the 12-sentence lead, else the whole article (no See also / References), else "does not say"; the engine now passes the user's question to search (<code>run(..., question=)</code>; cache key includes it). 12 cases + all earlier search tests pass (<code>temp/n70_when_probe.py</code>). <b>built 10-20 (Glenn), to-test ON THE GPU when WSL RAM allows:</b> one-click "Memory test" button = <code>Engine.memtest</code> / <code>POST /memtest</code>: the trainer's cross-chunk recall test (8 word pairs at the start of chunk 1, ~1,070 words of text, the key at word 1,089 in chunk 2; 20 tries, memory on vs off; one try shown as words). Logic checked with a stand-in model (<code>temp/n70_memtest_check.py</code>), page JS syntax OK; the real model is untested (final-model eval: 99-100% on, 1.6-12.5% off). <b>built 10-20 (Glenn), to-test on the GPU:</b> paste-able memory prompts <code>scripts/demo/memory_prompts/{A,B}.txt</code> + README (8 pairs in the training's token ranges, one exact token each, then ordinary text to 1,036 tokens; a typed key lands at token ~1,036+ in attention chunk 2) by <code>temp/n70_mk_memory_prompts.py</code>; token stream simulated (<code>temp/n70_memprompt_check.py</code>); raw mode now adds the joining space before a typed next word; filler words "carts"/"smelled" (not in the 32k vocab) replaced. <b>idea (parked, next SFT):</b> the model still writes America/New_York for "California" (guard corrects it, shown on the page): tools.jsonl teaches get_time only with IANA names (Cairo 180 