  <li><b>10-15 21:20 (Glenn) CHECKPOINT-AVERAGE SPACING TEST for the final SFT base</b>. Literature: PMA (ByteDance 2505.12082) best interval ~4B tok for 0.7B, more checkpoints help once training ends; Early Weight Averaging (Sanyal 2306.03241) gains grow with wider spacing at HIGH LR; WSM: total window (merge duration) matters most; Baichuan2 merge study: distant checkpoints can hurt. Our run ends at the cosine floor (low LR) &rarr; gains likely smaller and wide windows may hurt &rarr; test. PLAN (proposed): <code>temp/n65_avg_spacing.sh</code> on the 5080 once the final is home (~03:30): candidates A final alone, B final+2 newest (window ~9k steps), C final+2nd+4th, D final+3rd+6th (~27k), E final+4 newest, F 6 newest; metric chunk ppl (chunk1 / chunks2+) + memory delta; winner list &rarr; <code>temp/n62_avg_list</code>, read by a small additive change to <code>temp/n62_mkbase.sh</code> (default = today&rsquo;s newest-k). No delay to B4; done long before <code>n62_final.sh</code>. Option: also save the 2 instance-only pre-final checkpoints (~318k / 319.5k) for a tight-spacing candidate. <b>Glenn OK 21:40 (both). BUILT + ARMED 20:55</b>: instance <code>temp_n65_extras.sh</code> (from <code>temp/n65_extras_remote.sh</code>) copies step_0318000 / 0319500 to <code>gdrive:neuro_v4_pinned/v4_cloud_conv_extra</code> as they appear (md5-checked, before the run ends, so no race with the autostop guard; log instance logs/n65_extras.log); home <code>temp/n65_avg_spacing.sh</code> (setsid, waits for the final = step 320739; pulls the extras to <code>v4_conv_extra</code>; arms A F / B tight 1.5k / C 4.5k / D 9k / E 13.5k / G k5 @4.5k / H tight+medium; one arm on disk at a time; DRY=&lt;step&gt; mode tested) &rarr; <code>temp/n62_avg_list_cF</code>; <code>temp/n62_mkbase.sh</code> reads it for cF only (absent = newest-k, B4 unchanged). If n62_final starts before the test ends it uses newest-k. <b>RESULT 05:20</b> (chunk1 / memory &Delta;): A final 20.17/+1.00 | B tight 18.76/+0.96 | C 18.57/+0.92 | D 18.59/+0.91 | E (Glenn&rsquo;s 3rd+6th) 18.77/+0.89 | <b>G k5 ~19k window 18.39/+0.92 (&minus;8.8%)</b> | H skipped. Wider/more wins &rarr; list = G; testing I (k7, ~30k) / J (k10, ~46k) by <code>temp/n65_avg_wider.sh</code> (replaces the list only if better). <b>05:28: I 18.40/+0.90, J 18.61/+0.84 &rarr; G stays (k5, ~19k window = the optimum here; past ~20k steps it flattens then worsens).</b> status: DONE. CORPUS: NOT needed (Glenn 21:15: already on Drive &gt; Computers &gt; My Computer &gt; neuro_corpus_v4); the instance copy was stopped at 6 GB and trashed. Drive pin loop (<code>n61_drive_pin_loop.sh</code>) STOPPED 21:10 to save Drive space (everything is pulled home; relaunch line in <code>temp/n65_stop_pinloop.sh</code>). RISK: G: 61 GiB free, vhdx 852 &rarr; 915 GB today.</li>
